    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The British Association for Islamic Studies (BRAIS) and De Gruyter have announced the outcome of the fifth (2020) round of the BRAIS - De Gruyter Prize in the Study of Islam and the Muslim World. The winning submission is Gowaart Van Den Bossche's PhD thesis on \"The Past, Panegyric, and the Performance of Penmanship: Sultanic Biography and Social Practice in Late Medieval Egypt and Syria\", which he defended in 2019 at Ghent University, right before joining the  KITAB project  as a postdoctoral fellow. In his own words:",
